The `kubectl edit` command failed because the default editor (`vi`) could not be launched in the execution environment. I must achieve the same goal by applying a patch or by providing the full, corrected manifest if possible, but since I cannot run an editor, I will use `kubectl patch` to make the minimal, justified change.

The minimal change is adding the `volumes` and the `volumeMount` to the existing container definition within the deployment spec.

**Patch Definition:**

I need to add:
1.  A volume named `temp-cache` of type `emptyDir` to `spec.template.spec.volumes`.
2.  A volume mount to `/var/cache/nginx` for the `app` container, referencing `temp-cache`.

I will use a JSON merge patch.

```json
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "volumes": [
          {
            "name": "temp-cache",
            "emptyDir": {}
          }
        ],
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "volumeMounts": [
              {
                "name": "temp-cache",
                "mountPath": "/var/cache/nginx"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

I will execute this patch.

